  "notes": "Modified cash basis village (treated as cash). Governmental lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (p5); fund balance roll-forward 243,656 + 302,467 - 349,825 + 120,000 = 316,298. Transfers: the Total column prints net 'Transfers in (out)' 120,000 (from the Enterprise Fund, p7); recorded gross by fund column as in FY2024: transfers_in Street 200,000, transfers_out General 80,000 (net 120,000). No beginning cash printed for governmental funds (no prior-year balance sheet); ending_cash = governmental funds 'Cash and cash equivalents' 148,793 and ending_investments = 'Certificates of deposit' 140,440 (p4); county treasurer cash 5,182 and restricted CDs 21,883 are separate lines. Business-type (single Enterprise Fund) from p7 (modified cash, ties to Statement of Activities p2-3: expenses 678,277, charges 794,665, miscellaneous 11,265, interest 5,852, transfers (120,000)): 499,759 + 811,782 - 678,277 - 120,000 = 513,264. Enterprise 'Other revenue' counted as general revenue Miscellaneous on the Statement of Activities, so category other. Capital outlay lines: no function printed (General Fund / Enterprise Fund), labelled 'Capital Outlay'. Proprietary cash flows set null (modified cash basis, as FY2024). Balance sheet: governmental lines from the governmental funds balance sheet (p4, total 316,298 equals government-wide), business-type from p1. Detail: the only schedule is the all-funds budgetary comparison (p9, function totals only), so detail is per-fund lines from the fund statements (p5, p7). Read pages 1-9 of 9"
